WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.337 --> 00:00:03.705
balloon high above the U.S. We

00:00:03.838 --> 00:00:05.406
reported on earlier is not the

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:06.407
only object in the sky people

00:00:06.541 --> 00:00:08.242
are talking about tonight.

00:00:08.376 --> 00:00:11.846
We just got this new image in of

00:00:11.979 --> 00:00:15.316
a historic event, a green comet

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:19.287
that has not been visible in the

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:21.856
sky since the stone age, about

00:00:21.989 --> 00:00:25.927
50,000 years ago, recently

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:29.664
photographed above stonehenge in

00:00:29.797 --> 00:00:29.997
England.

00:00:30.131 --> 00:00:31.733
It is a rare and historic treat

00:00:31.866 --> 00:00:32.900
to see it.

00:00:32.934 --> 00:00:36.904
I'm joined by Adam frank,

00:00:36.971 --> 00:00:39.941
professor of physics.

00:00:40.074 --> 00:00:41.409
How significant is this comet,

00:00:41.542 --> 00:00:43.211
and did you get a chance to see

00:00:43.344 --> 00:00:43.945
it yourself?

00:00:44.078 --> 00:00:45.380
&gt;&gt; The thing that's really cool

00:00:45.513 --> 00:00:46.581
about this is time.

00:00:46.914 --> 00:00:48.916
If you think about the comet as

00:00:48.916 --> 00:00:50.918
like a clock, then the last time

00:00:50.918 --> 00:00:52.920
that the hands were pointing to

00:00:52.954 --> 00:00:57.291
where it is now was the ice age,

00:00:57.425 --> 00:00:58.926
essentially, when there was two

00:00:59.026 --> 00:01:01.996
miles of ice above my head and

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:04.532
the entire world's population

00:01:04.932 --> 00:01:06.033
could fit into Cleveland.

00:01:06.167 --> 00:01:08.269
What this shows us is these

00:01:08.403 --> 00:01:10.071
comets are visitors from the

00:01:10.204 --> 00:01:11.739
dawn of time in many ways.

00:01:11.873 --> 00:01:13.207
It's such an amazing thing to

00:01:13.341 --> 00:01:15.042
think about the last time this

00:01:15.176 --> 00:01:17.078
comet went by, it was all

00:01:17.211 --> 00:01:18.246
forests, and now it's New York

00:01:18.379 --> 00:01:20.481
City and tiktok.

00:01:20.615 --> 00:01:23.384
&gt;&gt; Well, I missed it last time

00:01:23.518 --> 00:01:26.521
and this time, so now I have to

00:01:26.954 --> 00:01:32.493
wait another 50,000 years?

00:01:32.627 --> 00:01:35.263
&gt;&gt; Well, a comet like this, it's

00:01:35.396 --> 00:01:37.031
possible this comet is going to

00:01:37.165 --> 00:01:38.566
leave, that actually

00:01:38.966 --> 00:01:39.934
interactions with Jupiter or

00:01:40.067 --> 00:01:42.036
Saturn are going to give it just

00:01:42.170 --> 00:01:43.304
enough energy that it's never

00:01:43.438 --> 00:01:44.338
coming back.

00:01:44.472 --> 00:01:47.542
&gt;&gt; It was just discovered last

00:01:47.675 --> 00:01:49.677
March, so how common is it to

00:01:49.811 --> 00:01:51.112
discover something that old?

00:01:51.245 --> 00:01:53.414
&gt;&gt; Well, there's two kinds of

00:01:53.548 --> 00:01:53.748
comets.

00:01:53.881 --> 00:01:55.716
There's the one that is come

00:01:55.850 --> 00:01:59.353
around less than every 200 years

00:01:59.487 --> 00:02:01.622
like haileys, every 75 years or

00:02:01.756 --> 00:02:01.889
so.

00:02:02.023 --> 00:02:04.258
But these comets are so far out

00:02:04.392 --> 00:02:05.993
that you really only catch them

00:02:06.127 --> 00:02:06.294
once.

00:02:06.427 --> 00:02:07.328
You catch them the first time

00:02:07.462 --> 00:02:09.664
that they're coming in because

00:02:09.797 --> 00:02:12.166
often they'll fall into the sun,

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:13.401
or once they're gone, they're

00:02:13.534 --> 00:02:15.970
not coming back forever or

00:02:16.103 --> 00:02:17.472
50,000 years.

00:02:17.605 --> 00:02:21.943
It's this new telescope

00:02:22.076 --> 00:02:23.744
technology that can pick up

00:02:23.878 --> 00:02:25.446
faint objects in the sky as they

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:26.013
change position.

00:02:26.147 --> 00:02:27.949
It's taking pictures of the

00:02:28.082 --> 00:02:29.884
entire sky every night.

00:02:30.017 --> 00:02:32.587
It's because of that transient

00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:34.255
telescope that we're able to

00:02:34.388 --> 00:02:35.690
catch more of these.

00:02:35.823 --> 00:02:37.992
Soon we'll be catching a lot

00:02:38.125 --> 00:02:40.628
more of these intruders from the

00:02:41.028 --> 00:02:41.062
solar system.

00:02:41.195 --> 00:02:44.532
&gt;&gt; I understand the comet can be

00:02:44.665 --> 00:02:46.067
differentiated from the stars

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:48.703
because it has that dust and

00:02:49.036 --> 00:02:49.537
energized particles around it as

00:02:49.670 --> 00:02:51.472
well as something called a green

00:02:51.606 --> 00:02:52.640
coma surrounding it.

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:55.610
What exactly is a coma in this

00:02:55.743 --> 00:02:56.577
context, and where does the

00:02:56.711 --> 00:02:57.545
green come from?

00:02:57.678 --> 00:02:59.680
&gt;&gt; So a comet is basically a

00:02:59.814 --> 00:03:01.782
giant mountain of mush, of

00:03:01.916 --> 00:03:03.718
frozen mush, and as it comes in

00:03:03.851 --> 00:03:05.553
towards the sun, it heats up,

00:03:05.686 --> 00:03:08.022
and as it heats up, the ices

00:03:08.155 --> 00:03:10.391
begin to melt and vaporize.

00:03:10.525 --> 00:03:13.060
So the coma is sort of this gas

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:14.395
and plasma that's surrounding

00:03:14.529 --> 00:03:17.064
the comet that just recently

00:03:17.064 --> 00:03:18.633
went from the ice state to the

00:03:19.066 --> 00:03:19.333
gas state.

00:03:19.467 --> 00:03:21.168
And the green comes from light

00:03:21.302 --> 00:03:23.271
from the sun ripping apart

00:03:23.404 --> 00:03:26.107
molecules like cyanide or

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:28.609
carbons -- two carbon atoms

00:03:28.743 --> 00:03:30.444
glued together, so that green

00:03:30.578 --> 00:03:32.780
hue is telling you the surface

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:35.082
of the comet is being torn apart

00:03:35.082 --> 00:03:36.183
from the intense light from the

00:03:36.317 --> 00:03:36.484
sun.

00:03:36.617 --> 00:03:38.119
&gt;&gt; Again, if you missed it this

00:03:38.252 --> 00:03:40.555
time, it may not exist in a few

00:03:40.688 --> 00:03:43.090
more years because it may get

00:03:43.224 --> 00:03:43.491
torn apart.

